.if \n[.g] .mso www.tmac
.TH SDL_X11EventHook 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_X11EventHook \- A callback to be used with
.BR SDL_SetX11EventHook .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_system.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef bool (SDLCALL *SDL_X11EventHook)(void *userdata, XEvent *xevent);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This callback may modify the event, and should return true if the event should continue to be processed, or false to prevent further processing\[char46]
.PP
As this is processing an event directly from the X11 event loop, this callback should do the minimum required work and return quickly\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I userdata
the app-defined pointer provided to
.BR SDL_SetX11EventHook \[char46]

.TP
.I xevent
a pointer to an Xlib XEvent union to process\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true to let event continue on, false to drop it\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This may only be called (by SDL) from the thread handling the X11 event loop\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This datatype is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetX11EventHook (3)
